serial sum correct: true
warp-shuffle sum parity: true
two-phase shuffle rendering (GPU) or serial fallback (CPU): true
warp-shuffle fma dot parity: true
single-warp shuffle rendering (GPU) or serial fallback (CPU): true
warp-shuffle max parity: true
non-warp-multiple extent rejected (GPU) or runs serially (CPU): true
guarded smaller-extent accumulation rejected (GPU) or runs serially (CPU): true
an unguarded accumulation nest under the Workgroup_reduce level (a Serial level inside it) is refused loudly where a lane index is bound (GPU) or localized whole as a serial nest (CPU): true
the bf16 single-warp rival-rendering values are pairwise distinct: true
the bf16 four-warp rival-rendering values are pairwise distinct: true
a bf16 single-warp Workgroup_reduce accumulates at the widened residency (32 terms narrow once to 33.25, not the 33 a bf16-staged tree or the 32.75 a per-step narrowing gives): true
a bf16 four-warp Workgroup_reduce stages its per-warp partials at the widened residency (128 terms narrow once to 133, not the 132 a bf16-staged tree or the 129 a per-step narrowing gives): true
the emitted shuffle declares its staging register and its per-warp slots at the residency type, never at bf16 storage: true
an f16 accumulator whose residency stays narrow, as the default fp16_arithmetic policy resolves it on every GPU backend, is refused by the warp-shuffle rendering (GPU) or runs serially (CPU): true
a bf16 Workgroup_reduce whose contribution mentions an RNG conversion is refused where the residency is wider than storage (GPU) or runs serially (CPU): true
the f16 single-warp rival-rendering values are pairwise distinct: true
the f16 four-warp rival-rendering values are pairwise distinct: true
under Fp16_wide an f16 single-warp Workgroup_reduce accumulates at the widened residency (32 terms narrow once to 32.15625, not the 32.125 an f16-staged tree or the 32.09375 a per-step narrowing gives): true
under Fp16_wide an f16 four-warp Workgroup_reduce stages its per-warp partials at the widened residency (128 terms narrow once to 128.625, not the 128.5 an f16-staged tree or the 128.125 a per-step narrowing gives): true
under Fp16_wide the emitted f16 shuffle declares its staging register and its per-warp slots at the residency type, never at half storage: true
a Workgroup_reduce level holding a sibling statement beside a lane-invariant self-updating Set is refused where a lane index is bound (GPU: the hardware binding would race the cell) or runs serially (CPU): true
a Workgroup_reduce level holding a data-dependent guard over a lane-invariant self-updating Set is refused where a lane index is bound (GPU: the guard leaves several lanes on the cell) or runs serially (CPU): true
a lane-invariant self-updating Set under a guard pinning the lane index to one value is not a race: the hardware binding renders it and one lane performs the update (GPU), or the serial loop admits the one iteration (CPU): true
